From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:32:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5CEMU-HAR's Switch side: in its app folder's eden/, back to
 it after a game

PS5CEMU-HAR (PPSA99360) carries this program as eden/eboot.bin and starts it with LoadExec.
- Its folder is the app's eden/ (/app0/eden, /system_ex/app/PPSA99360/eden,
  /data/homebrew/PPSA99360/eden), its sandbox PPSA99360's, its data /data/ps5cemu/eden. The game
  files folder is /data/ps5cemu/eden by default; while that has no keys, a standalone ProsperoEden's
  /data/prosperoeden is used as it is when it has them.
- Where main returns (its launcher left, or a game PS5CEMU-HAR started with --rom has ended), it
  LoadExecs PS5CEMU-HAR's eboot (--return <eboot>, then /app0, the system's mount and
  /data/homebrew) instead of closing; a home screen tile's --exit-after-game still closes it.
  Circle on the home screen leaves the launcher. After a crash it starts itself again
  (/app0/eden/eboot.bin), whose launcher shows the crash notice.
- A game started with --rom gets its cover and its own name in covers/, as the library keeps them,
  for PS5CEMU-HAR's Switch side to show.
- The Lapy helper is built for PPSA99360.
